1
00:00:01,756 --> 00:00:05,914
Chapter 74. The sperm whale's head.

2
00:00:05,915 --> 00:00:08,719
contrasted view.

3
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:14,159
Here now are two great whales laying their heads together. Let us join them

4
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:20,399
and lay together our own. Of the grand order of folio leviathans, the sperm

5
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:25,359
whale and the right whale are by far the most noteworthy. They are the only

6
00:00:25,360 --> 00:00:30,719
whales regularly hunted by man. To the Nantucketer, they present the two

7
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:35,999
extremes of all the known varieties of the whale, as the external difference

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:41,115
between them is mainly observable in their heads, and as a head of each is

9
00:00:41,116 --> 00:00:46,558
this moment hanging from the Peekquad's side, and as we may freely go from one

10
00:00:46,559 --> 00:00:51,359
to the other by merely stepping across the deck, where I should like to know,

11
00:00:51,360 --> 00:00:56,954
will you obtain a better chance to study practical Slogy than here?

12
00:00:56,955 --> 00:01:01,039
In the first place, you are struck by the general contrast between these

13
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:06,159
heads. Both are massive enough in all conscience, but there is a certain

14
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:10,558
mathematical symmetry in the sperm whales, which the right whales sadly

15
00:01:10,559 --> 00:01:15,755
lacks. There is more character in the sperm whale's head. As you behold it,

16
00:01:15,756 --> 00:01:21,435
you involuntarily yield the immense superiority to him in point of pervading

17
00:01:21,436 --> 00:01:26,878
dignity. In the present instance too, this dignity is heightened by the pepper

18
00:01:26,879 --> 00:01:32,558
and salt color of his head at the summit, giving token of advanced age and

19
00:01:32,559 --> 00:01:41,435
large experience. In short, he is what the fishermen technically call a gayheaded whale.

20
00:01:41,436 --> 00:01:46,878
Let us now note what is least dissimilar in these heads, namely the two most

21
00:01:46,879 --> 00:01:50,159
important organs, the eye and the ear.

22
00:01:50,160 --> 00:01:54,719
far back on the side of the head, and low down near the angle of either

23
00:01:54,720 --> 00:02:00,638
whale's jaw, if you narrowly search, you will at last see a lashless eye, which

24
00:02:00,639 --> 00:02:05,518
you would fancy to be a young colt's eye, so out of all proportion is it to

25
00:02:05,519 --> 00:02:08,318
the magnitude of the head.

26
00:02:08,319 --> 00:02:13,838
Now, from this peculiar sideway position of the whale's eyes, it is plain that he

27
00:02:13,839 --> 00:02:19,274
can never see an object which is exactly ahead, no more than he can one exactly a

28
00:02:19,275 --> 00:02:24,878
stern. In a word, the position of the whale's eyes corresponds to that of a

29
00:02:24,879 --> 00:02:29,679
man's ears, and you may fancy for yourself how it would fare with you did

30
00:02:29,680 --> 00:02:34,638
you sideways survey objects through your ears. You would find that you could only

31
00:02:34,639 --> 00:02:40,479
command some 30° of vision in advance of the straight sideline of sight and about

32
00:02:40,480 --> 00:02:45,679
30 more behind it. If your bitterest foe were walking straight towards you with

33
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:50,799
dagger uplifted in broad day, you would not be able to see him any more than if

34
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:53,435
he were stealing upon you from behind.

35
00:02:53,436 --> 00:02:58,799
In a word, you would have two backs, so to speak, but at the same time also two

36
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:04,954
fronts, side fronts. For what is it that makes the front of a man what indeed but

37
00:03:04,955 --> 00:03:07,274
his eyes?

38
00:03:07,275 --> 00:03:12,079
Moreover, while in most other animals that I can now think of, the eyes are so

39
00:03:12,080 --> 00:03:17,115
planted as imperceptibly to blend their visual power, so as to produce one

40
00:03:17,116 --> 00:03:21,999
picture and not two, to the brain, the peculiar position of the whale's eyes,

41
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:28,159
effectually divided, as they are by many cubic feet of solid head, which towers

42
00:03:28,160 --> 00:03:33,274
between them like a great mountain separating two lakes in valleys. This of

43
00:03:33,275 --> 00:03:37,594
course must wholly separate the impressions which each independent organ

44
00:03:37,595 --> 00:03:42,799
imparts. The whale therefore must see one distinct picture on this side and

45
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:47,274
another distinct picture on that side, while all between must be profound

46
00:03:47,275 --> 00:03:52,799
darkness and nothingness to him. Man may in effect be said to look out on the

47
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:57,914
world from a sentry box with two joined sashes for his window. But for the

48
00:03:57,915 --> 00:04:03,435
whale, these two sashes are separately inserted, making two distinct windows,

49
00:04:03,436 --> 00:04:08,479
but sadly impairing the view. This peculiarity of the whale's eyes is a

50
00:04:08,480 --> 00:04:12,638
thing always to be borne in mind in the fishery, and to be remembered by the

51
00:04:12,639 --> 00:04:16,479
reader in some subsequent scenes.

52
00:04:16,480 --> 00:04:20,954
A curious and most puzzling question might be started concerning this visual

53
00:04:20,955 --> 00:04:26,558
matter as touching the Leviathan, but I must be content with a hint. So long as

54
00:04:26,559 --> 00:04:31,914
a man's eyes are open in the light, the act of seeing is involuntary, that is,

55
00:04:31,915 --> 00:04:36,399
he cannot help mechanically seeing whatever objects are before him.

56
00:04:36,400 --> 00:04:40,878
Nevertheless, anyone's experience will teach him that though he can take in an

57
00:04:40,879 --> 00:04:46,159
undiscriminating sweep of things at one glance, it is quite impossible for him

58
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:51,755
attentively and completely, to examine any two things, however large or however

59
00:04:51,756 --> 00:04:57,115
small, at one in the same instant of time. Never mind if they lie side by

60
00:04:57,116 --> 00:05:02,159
side and touch each other. But if you now come to separate these two objects

61
00:05:02,160 --> 00:05:06,799
and surround each by a circle of profound darkness, then in order to see

62
00:05:06,800 --> 00:05:09,198
one of them in such a manner as to bring

63
00:05:09,199 --> 00:05:13,274
your mind to bear on it, the other will be utterly excluded from your

64
00:05:13,275 --> 00:05:18,638
contemporary consciousness. How is it then with the whale? True, both his eyes

65
00:05:18,639 --> 00:05:21,914
in themselves must simultaneously act.

66
00:05:21,915 --> 00:05:26,079
But is his brain so much more comprehensive, combining, and subtle

67
00:05:26,080 --> 00:05:31,518
than man's that he can at the same moment of time attentively examine two

68
00:05:31,519 --> 00:05:37,198
distinct prospects, one on one side of him and the other in an exactly opposite

69
00:05:37,199 --> 00:05:42,558
direction? If he can, then is it a marvelous thing in him, as if a man were

70
00:05:42,559 --> 00:05:47,198
able to simultaneously go through the demonstrations of two distinct problems

71
00:05:47,199 --> 00:05:55,274
in Uklid, nor strictly investigated, is there any inongruity in this comparison,

72
00:05:55,275 --> 00:05:59,594
it may be but an idle whim, but it has always seemed to me that the

73
00:05:59,595 --> 00:06:04,638
extraordinary vacasillations of movement displayed by some whales when beset by

74
00:06:04,639 --> 00:06:10,238
three or four boats, the timidity and liability to queer frights so common to

75
00:06:10,239 --> 00:06:14,878
such whales. I think that all this indirectly proceeds from the helpless

76
00:06:14,879 --> 00:06:19,518
perplexity of volition in which their divided and diametrically opposite

77
00:06:19,519 --> 00:06:23,115
powers of vision must involve them.

78
00:06:23,116 --> 00:06:28,558
But the ear of the whale is full as curious as the eye. If you are an entire

79
00:06:28,559 --> 00:06:33,359
stranger to their race, you might hunt over these two heads for hours and never

80
00:06:33,360 --> 00:06:39,115
discover that organ. The ear has no external leaf whatever, and into the

81
00:06:39,116 --> 00:06:44,954
hole itself you can hardly insert a quill, so wondrously minute is it. It is

82
00:06:44,955 --> 00:06:49,755
lodged a little behind the eye. With respect to their ears, this important

83
00:06:49,756 --> 00:06:54,399
difference is to be observed between the sperm whale and the right, while the ear

84
00:06:54,400 --> 00:06:57,039
of the former has an external opening.

85
00:06:57,040 --> 00:07:01,838
That of the latter is entirely and evenly covered over with a membrane, so

86
00:07:01,839 --> 00:07:05,518
as to be quite imperceptible from without.

87
00:07:05,519 --> 00:07:10,159
Is it not curious that so vast a being as the whale should see the world

88
00:07:10,160 --> 00:07:14,799
through so small an eye and hear the thunder through an ear which is smaller

89
00:07:14,800 --> 00:07:20,878
than a hairs? But if the eye were broad as the lens of Hersel's great telescope

90
00:07:20,879 --> 00:07:25,838
and his ears capacious as the porches of cathedrals, would that make him any

91
00:07:25,839 --> 00:07:28,719
longer of sight or sharper of hearing?

92
00:07:28,720 --> 00:07:36,954
Not at all. Why then do you try to enlarge your mind? Subtalize it.

93
00:07:36,955 --> 00:07:42,079
Let us now, with whatever levers and steam engines we have at hand, can't

94
00:07:42,080 --> 00:07:47,274
over the sperm whale's head, that it may lie bottom up, then ascending by a

95
00:07:47,275 --> 00:07:52,159
ladder to the summit, have a peep down the mouth. And were it not that the body

96
00:07:52,160 --> 00:07:56,558
is now completely separated from it, with a lantern, we might descend into

97
00:07:56,559 --> 00:08:02,238
the great Kentucky mammoth cave of the stomach, but let us hold on here by this

98
00:08:02,239 --> 00:08:05,115
tooth and look about us where we are.

99
00:08:05,116 --> 00:08:09,594
What a really beautiful and chastel looking mouth from floor to ceiling,

100
00:08:09,595 --> 00:08:16,719
lined, or rather papered with a glistening white membrane, glossy as bridal satins.

101
00:08:16,720 --> 00:08:21,274
But come out now and look at this portentious lower jaw which seems like

102
00:08:21,275 --> 00:08:27,115
the long narrow lid of an immense snuff box with the hinge at one end instead of

103
00:08:27,116 --> 00:08:32,954
one side. If you pry it up so as to get it overhead and expose its rows of

104
00:08:32,955 --> 00:08:39,039
teeth, it seems a terrific portal. And such, alas, it proves to many a poor

105
00:08:39,040 --> 00:08:45,039
white in the fishery upon whom these spikes fall with impaling force. But far

106
00:08:45,040 --> 00:08:50,079
more terrible is it to behold when fathoms down in the sea you see some

107
00:08:50,080 --> 00:08:56,318
sulky whale floating there suspended with his predigious jaw some 15 ft long

108
00:08:56,319 --> 00:09:01,274
hanging straight down at right angles with his body for all the world like a

109
00:09:01,275 --> 00:09:10,079
ship's jib boom this whale is not dead he is only dispirited out of sorts perhaps hypocchondric

110
00:09:10,080 --> 00:09:15,755
and so supine that the hinges of his jaw have relaxed leaving him there in that

111
00:09:15,756 --> 00:09:21,039
ungainainely sort of plight, a reproach to all his tribe, who must no doubt

112
00:09:21,040 --> 00:09:24,719
imprecate lock jaws upon him.

113
00:09:24,720 --> 00:09:30,719
In most cases, this lower jaw, being easily unhinged by a practiced artist,

114
00:09:30,720 --> 00:09:35,274
is disengaged and hoisted on deck for the purpose of extracting the ivory

115
00:09:35,275 --> 00:09:40,238
teeth, and furnishing a supply of that hard white whale bone with which the

116
00:09:40,239 --> 00:09:45,274
fishermen fashion all sorts of curious articles, including canes, umbrella

117
00:09:45,275 --> 00:09:48,399
stocks, and handles to riding whips.

118
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:53,198
With a long, weary hoist, the jaw is dragged on board as if it were an

119
00:09:53,199 --> 00:09:58,399
anchor. And when the proper time comes, some few days after the other work,

120
00:09:58,400 --> 00:10:03,518
Quiqu Dagu, and Tashego, all being accomplished dentists, are set to

121
00:10:03,519 --> 00:10:09,359
drawing teeth. With a keen cutting spade, Quiquay lances the gums. Then the

122
00:10:09,360 --> 00:10:13,999
jaw is lashed down to ring bolts, and a tackle being rigged from a loft. They

123
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:19,435
drag out these teeth, as Michigan oxmen drag stumps of old oaks out of wild

124
00:10:19,436 --> 00:10:26,079
woodlands. There are generally 42 teeth in all. in old whales much worn down but

125
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:32,719
undeayed nor filled after our artificial fashion. The jaw is afterwards sawn into

126
00:10:32,720 --> 00:10:38,756
slabs and piled away like joists for building houses.
